q 1 0 0 1 51.35433 778.3701 cm .101961 .101961 .180392 rg BT/F2 12 Tf 0 3 TD (Caption protocol in the E-series)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 51.35433 633.5701 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 2.570015 Tw/F1 9.3 Tf 0 131.5 TD (COCO supplies )Tj/F2 9.3 Tf (five independent human captions per image)Tj/F1 9.3 Tf (, written by five annotators; five is the dataset's)Tj 1.372575 Tw 0 -12.800003 TD (structure, not a tuned choice. The decision was whether to use one or all. A single caption carries that annotator's)Tj 1.864746 Tw T* (emphasis - one names the activity, another the setting - so the target vector mixes image content with individual)Tj .577871 Tw T* (phrasing. Averaging the five embeddings cancels the idiosyncrasies and keeps what they agree on, making the target)Tj .396439 Tw T* ('what the image is about' rather than 'what one person wrote'. The effect is large: held-out R2 rises 0.278 to 0.511 and)Tj 1.230476 Tw T* (R@1 0.160 to 0.358. The same averaging must be applied to the ceiling, because it makes the task easier for any)Tj 1.607361 Tw 0 -12.799999 TD (method - SigLIP itself scores 0.648 on single captions and 0.875 on averaged ones. Scoring an averaged system)Tj 1.607908 Tw T* (against a single-caption ceiling produced an inflated 55.2 )Tj[-4063.8948]TJ ( matched properly it is 40.9. Both protocols are)Tj .241439 Tw T* (reported, and both fall in the same pre-registered band \(24.7 and 40.9 )Tj[-4249.9616]TJ ( so the verdict does not depend on the)Tj 1.182296 Tw T* (choice; note that the standard COCO benchmark convention is one caption per query, so averaging is a deliberate,)Tj 0 Tw 0 -12.8 TD (disclosed deviation.)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 51.35433 609.5701 cm .101961 .101961 .180392 rg BT/F2 12 Tf 0 3 TD (A note on alpha)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 51.35433 528.7701 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 1.227127 Tw/F1 9.3 Tf 0 67.5 TD (ALPHA_GRID in the E-series is a )Tj/F2 9.3 Tf (search over regularization strength)Tj/F1 9.3 Tf (, not a learning-rate schedule: ridge has no)Tj .851036 Tw 0 -12.799999 TD (training loop,